cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Ikarus in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Ikarus: High-Precision 2-D RCWA Simulation for Periodic Photonic Structures"
abstract: >-
  Ikarus is a high-precision 2-D rigorous coupled-wave analysis (RCWA / Fourier
  Modal Method) solver for periodic photonic structures -- metasurfaces, gratings,
  photonic-crystal slabs, thin-film stacks and metamirrors. It uses faithful
  Fourier factorization (the normal-vector / Fast-Fourier-Factorization method by
  default) for correct high-index-contrast TM convergence, with full vectorial
  polarization, anisotropic media, real-space field reconstruction and
  gradient-based inverse design.
